			<div class="content" id="post-content-2320434">
									

<blockquote>
<p>2221-A populations tend to be densely clustered,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think the description should go into a least a little detail on how the clustering happens.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>POP-044-2221-A distributes print versions of SCP-2221, thereby converting nearly all adult members of affected communities into instances of 2221-A.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If the three anomaly-causing clauses can be put into printed documents which get signed, then the description shouldn't say &quot;<em>An instance of SCP-2221 is an End User License Agreement (EULA)</em>&quot;. Perhaps you mean to imply one or both of the following:</p>
<ol>
<li>That for any given infected area, the infection always starts via the EULA vector.</li>
<li>That the modification of EULAs appear to happen spontaneously, without the intervention of any instances of 2221-A.</li>
</ol>
<p>If so, you should make that explicit.</p>
<p>Also, if this affects EULA for downloaded software, why not also the terms of agreement for signing up on websites?</p>
<p>Also also: this has limited potential to spread in areas with low literacy rates, so I would think that 2221-A would encourage teaching literacy.</p>

